questions.question:
What is the output of the following code?
```python
class A:
    def method(self): return 'A'
class B(A): pass
class C(B):
    def method(self): return 'C' + super().method()

print(C().method())
print(B().method())
```

questions.answer:
The outputs are CA and A. super() in C follows the MRO past B (which has no override) to A.

